# Cursor & AI Agent Rules for Run Escape

1. MANDATORY PRE-READ: Always read `AGENTS.md`, `AGENT_NOTES.md`, and `.jules/sentinel.md` before editing any files or resolving merges.
2. SOURCE-FIRST WORKFLOW: Edit TypeScript engine source in `src/` and compile via `npm run build` (`vite build && node scripts/sync_dist.cjs`). Never hand-edit or regex-patch minified bundles in `assets/index-*.js`.
3. CACHE-BUSTING LOCKSTEP: Whenever client JS, WASM, or CSS files change, run `npm run build` (or `node scripts/sync_dist.cjs --version=X.Y`) to synchronize the `?v=X.Y` query parameter across `index.html` and `assets/`.
4. MANDATORY HANDOFF LOG: Before finishing any task, commit, or PR, update `CHANGELOG.md` and prepend a new entry to `AGENT_NOTES.md` under `## 3. Chronological Agent Handoff Log` detailing modified files, bundle/symbol changes, and notes for future agents.
5. VERIFICATION: Run `npm test`, `python -m unittest test_serve.py`, and `node --check assets/multiplayer.js` prior to completion.
